#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rnsbox-sysupdate — RNSBox A/B whole-OS update agent.

Checks a user-configured repository (github-releases or generic manifest) for
a newer RNSBox image, and applies it by writing the IDLE rootfs slot of the
A/B layout, then flipping the slot pointer. Never touches the running slot;
the boot chain's boot-count rollback (initramfs + S98confirm) reverts a slot
that fails to boot healthy 3 times.

Design notes (see docs/AUTO-UPDATE.md):
  * crash-safe by construction: download -> verify sha256 -> write idle slot
    -> refresh boot files (old copies kept) -> flip -> reboot. A power cut
    anywhere before the flip leaves the running system untouched.
  * schedule: after every check the next check is drawn uniformly from
    [interval_min_days, interval_max_days] (default 7..14) and stored as
    next_check in /etc/rnsbox/update.conf — a fresh jitter each time, so a
    fleet of routers never polls in sync.
  * pure stdlib; no shell ever sees a URL; all writes are tmp-file + fsync +
    rename. Signature verification (ed25519, generic provider) is optional.
  * the physical topology (boot dir, slot devices) comes from probe_layout(),
    which honours RNSBOX_UPDATE_DEVMAP for tests/QEMU.

Commands:
  tick [--bg]         cron/boot entry: reconcile, check if due, maybe auto-apply
  check [--bg]        check now (refresh candidate + redraw next_check)
  apply [--bg] [--allow-unknown-version]   apply the current candidate
  reconcile           settle a pending flip into applied/rolled-back
  status              print the volatile state JSON
  enable|disable      write enabled=yes|no into update.conf
"""

